*> ACCOUNT-INT: reads a fixed-width account file, computes interest (3.5%)
      *> and writes a fixed-width result file. Copybook: copybook.cpy.
      *> Compile: cobc -free -x ACCOUNT-INT.cbl -o acct_int
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. ACCOUNT-INT.
ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
FILE-CONTROL.
    SELECT IN-FILE ASSIGN TO "ACCOUNTS.DAT"
        ORGANIZATION IS LINE SEQUENTIAL.
    SELECT OUT-FILE ASSIGN TO "OUT-COBOL.DAT"
        ORGANIZATION IS LINE SEQUENTIAL.
DATA DIVISION.
FILE SECTION.
FD  IN-FILE.
01  IN-REC.
    05 ACCT-NO   PIC 9(9).
    05 BAL       PIC 9(9)V99.
FD  OUT-FILE.
01  OUT-REC.
    05 O-ACCT    PIC 9(9).
    05 O-BAL     PIC 9(9)V99.
    05 O-INT     PIC 9(9)V99.
    05 O-NEWBAL  PIC 9(9)V99.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01  WS-INTEREST PIC 9(9)V99.
01  WS-NEWBAL   PIC 9(9)V99.
01  WS-EOF      PIC X VALUE 'N'.
01  WS-RATE     PIC 9V999 VALUE 0.035.
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
MAIN.
    OPEN INPUT IN-FILE.
    OPEN OUTPUT OUT-FILE.
    PERFORM UNTIL WS-EOF = 'Y'
        READ IN-FILE
            AT END MOVE 'Y' TO WS-EOF
            NOT AT END
                COMPUTE WS-INTEREST ROUNDED = BAL * WS-RATE
                COMPUTE WS-NEWBAL = BAL + WS-INTEREST
                MOVE ACCT-NO TO O-ACCT
                MOVE BAL TO O-BAL
                MOVE WS-INTEREST TO O-INT
                MOVE WS-NEWBAL TO O-NEWBAL
                WRITE OUT-REC
        END-READ
    END-PERFORM.
    CLOSE IN-FILE.
    CLOSE OUT-FILE.
    STOP RUN.